ʼs herdsmen and said, “The water is ours!” So he named the well Esek, because they contended with him.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"From there Abram moved on to the hill country east of Bethel and pitched his tent, with Bethel to the west and Ai to the east. There he built an altar to the Lord, and he called on the name of the Lord.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“The Lordhas greatly blessed my master, and he has become rich. He has given him sheep and cattle, silver and gold, menservants and maidservants, camels and donkeys.","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":112,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Hallelujah! Blessed is the man who fears the LORD, who greatly delights in His commandments.","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":112,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Wealth and riches are in his house, and his righteousness endures forever.","from":2},{"book":"JER","chapter":29,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then you will call upon Me and come and pray to Me, and I will listen to you.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Abram traveled through the land as far as the site of the Oak of Moreh at Shechem. And at that time the Canaanites were in the land.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"8-13":{"people":[{"id":"lot-h3876g","name":"Lot","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Haran","count":4,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"f