 front of unbelievers!","from":8},{"book":"1CO","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The very fact that you have lawsuits among you means that you are thoroughly defeated already. Why not rather be wronged? Why not rather be cheated?","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":19,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So when God destroyed the cities of the plain, He remembered Abraham, and He brought Lot out of the catastrophe that destroyed the cities where he had lived.","from":12},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The next day he came upon two Israelites who were fighting, and he tried to reconcile them, saying, ‘Men, you are brothers. Why are you mistreating each other?’","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the king of Sodom, the king of Gomorrah, the king of Admah, the king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (that is, Zoar) marched out and arrayed themselves for battle in the Valley of Siddim","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They also carried off Abramʼs nephew Lot and his possessions, since Lot was living in Sodom.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":19,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the two angels arrived at Sodom in the evening, and Lot was sitting in the gateway of the city. When Lot saw them, he got up to meet them, bowed facedown,","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"14-18":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"lot-h3876g","name":"Lot","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Haran","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"mamre-h4471g","name":"Mamre","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"words":[{"base":"H2233","lemma":"זֶ֫רַע","tr":"ze·ra","gloss":"seed","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":229},{"base":"H4487","lemma":"מָנָה","tr":"ma·nah","gloss":"to count","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"H0087","lemma":"אַבְרָם","tr":"av·ram","gloss":"Abram","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":61},{"base":"H6083","lemma":"עָפָר","tr":"a·phar","gloss":"dust","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":110},{"base":"H0167","lemma":"אָהַל","tr":"a·hal","gloss":"to pitch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H9031","lemma":"ךָּ","tr":"ka","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":727},{"base":"H0436","lemma":"אֵלוֹן","tr":"e·lon","gloss":"(Diviners') Oak","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H4471","lemma":"מַמְרֵא","tr":"mam·re","gloss":"Mamre","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H8033","lemma":"שָׁם","tr":"sham","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":834},{"base":"H0859","lemma":"אַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"you(m.s.)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1092}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CH","chapter":20,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Our God, did You not drive out the inhabitants of this land before Your people Israel and give it forever to the descendants of Abraham Your friend?","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":8,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then Noah built an altar to the Lord. And taking from every kind of clean animal and clean bird, he offered burnt offerings on the altar.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then an escapee came and reported this to Abram the Hebrew. Now Abram was living near the Oaks of Mamre the Amorite, a brother of Eshcol and Aner, all of whom were bound by treaty to Abram.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"On that day the Lordmade a covenant with Abram, saying, “To your descendants I have given this land—from the river of Egypt to the great River Euphrates—","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":18,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abraham by the Oaks of Mamre in the heat of the day, while he was sitting at the entrance of his tent.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The land that I gave to Abraham and Isaac I will give to you, and I will give this land to your descendants after you.”","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Jacob returned to his father Isaac at Mamre, near Kiriath-arba (that is, Hebron), where Abraham and Isaac had stayed.","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}